# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_8930012> (internal primary capillary plexus of median eminence)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:1571958") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:2891718") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://basicmedicalkey.com/endocrine-system-3/") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://purl.org/ccf/ASCTB-TEMP_internal-primary-capillary-plexus-of-median-eminence") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_8930012> "A capillary plexus located in the internal (deeper) zone of the median eminence, where neurosecretory terminals from hypothalamic neurons release regulatory hormones. This capillary network forms the initial collection point of the hypothalamo-hypophyseal portal system, receiving hypothalamic releasing and inhibiting hormones before they are transported via portal vessels to the anterior pituitary. The internal plexus is distinguished from the external plexus by its deeper position within the median eminence structure and its proximity to the primary neurosecretory terminals.")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002175> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_8930012> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_9606>)
